, WCA competition has received far more applications than it can accommodate, and it is frequently the case that there are not enough applicants to accommodate all of them.\r\nTo alleviate this situation, we aim to increase the total number of participants by holding series competitions in different regions at the same time.\r\nPlease register for one of Go x Go Kyoto 2023 or Tokyo Challenge Winter A\/B\/C 2023, whichever is most convenient for you.\r\n\r\n### WCA Series Competitions\r\nWCA series Competitions are a series of multiple competitions, and you can only participate in one of them.\r\nIf you apply for more than one series, only the one with the earliest application date will be accepted, and the others will be invalid.\r\n\r\nTokyo Challenge Winter A 2023 (**hereinafter referred to as \"Competition A**\") (https:\/\/www.worldcubeassociation.org\/competitions\/TokyoChallengeWinterA2023), Tokyo Challenge Winter B 2023 (**Competition B**) (https:\/\/www.worldcubeassociation.org\/competitions\/TokyoChallengeWinterB2023) and Tokyo Challenge Winter C 2023 (**This Competition \/ Competition C**)  are WCA series competitions.\r\nYou can participate in only one of the A, B and C competitions.\r\n\r\n### Requirements for non-competitors\r\nDue to the new coronavirus infection (COVID-19) control measures, the number of visitors to the venue will be limited.\r\nNo one will be allowed to enter the venue on the day of the event without any prior permission.\r\n\r\nDue to the limited area of the venue and to prevent the spread of infectious diseases, there are restrictions on the number of accompanying persons and observers.\r\nOne accompanying person is allowed for each competitor who is a minor (18 years old or younger) or requires special consideration (free of charge).\r\nVisitors other than the above-mentioned accompanying persons who wish to come and observe the event (hereinafter referred to as \"visitors\") will be charged a fee (1,000 yen). Due to the size of the venue, admission to visitors may be limited (in principle, visitors are accepted in the order of application. If the number of applicants reaches the limit, no visitors will be allowed.)\r\n\r\n### Supporters Wanted\r\nIn order to make Speed Cubing Challenge more sustainable and stable, we need people to support the event. Therefore, we would like to ask competitors and parents of competitors who are interested in supporting the event to become \"supporters\". The role of a supporter on the day of the event will be to set up the venue, reception, call-outs, input and print records, disinfect the tables, and clean up. Supporters are asked to cooperate within the scope that does not affect their own competitions or their children's competitions.\r\nWe will inform you of how to apply for supporters at a later date.\r\n","externalWebsite":"https:\/\/speedcubing.or.jp\/competition\/TokyoChallengeWinterC2023\/"},{"id":"TokyoOpen2006","name":"Tokyo Open 2006","city":"Tokyo","country":"JP","date":{"from":"2023-06-25 17:38:37","till":"2023-06-25 17:38:37"},"isCanceled":false,"events":["222","333","333bf","444","555"],"wcaDelegate":"[{Masayuki Akimoto (\u79cb\u5143\u6b63\u884c)}{mailto:masayuki@akimoto3.com}]","organiser":"[{JRCA\u95a2\u897f\u652f\u90e8}{mailto:jrcakansai@gmail.com}]","venue":{"name":"","address":"","details":"","coordinates":{"latitude":35.689487,"longitude":139.691706}},"information":"","externalWebsite":"http:\/\/jrca.cc\/taikai\/2006\/tokyo20060730a.htm"},{"id":"TokyoOpen2008","name":"Tokyo Open 2008","city":"Tokyo","country":"JP","date":{"from":"2023-06-25 17:38:37","till":"2023-06-25 17:38:37"},"isCanceled":false,"events":["222","333","333bf","333ft","333oh","444","555","magic","pyram"],"wcaDelegate":"[{Masayuki Akimoto (\u79cb\u5143\u6b63\u884c)}{mailto:masayuki@akimoto3.com}] [{Yuji Suse (\u5de3\u702c\u96c4\u53f2)}{mailto:ochamee@gmail.com}]","organiser":null,"venue":{"name":"[Ota Civic Hall](http:\/\/www.city.ota.tokyo.jp\/shisetsu\/hall\/kumin_c\